Z||000008||8Ball||11-01-2001||07:33 PM||||Ok a history lesson as I know it.<P>(Simple disclaimer: not trying to upset anyone just clear up a point)<P>Satan a.k.a. Lucifer Yes has always been a part of the christian belief system. But the reason so many people stereotype Wiccans as Devil worshippers comes from the Pagan god Pan. When the Christian armies were converting Those of the Olde Religion (mostly Druids). They Decided they had to build chruches so they could get the Druids to worship Christianity. These chruches were built on top of the Worship areas of the Druids. This was an attempt to make them understand they had no chice in the matter. Only problem they had was the only craftsmen they could find were the very Druids they were converting. So these Druid craftsmen carved depictions of there own god pan into the walls and ceilings of the churchs. Being rather upset at this the Christians then made an excuse for pan to be in there church. He became the first documented image of Satan.<P>Several hundred years ago we were all in the dark ages and I personally believe this was christianities dark age. I am glad we have ALL grown beyond this point.<P>Sorry so long, and as I stated befor this was not meant to upset anyone. Just meant to clarify why We as Wiccans are thought by so many to be satanist.<P>Of coarse the mockery called the witch hunts, in which if you didn't like someone call them a witch and have them killed, didn't help much either.<P>Randy W.||||reg||1
Z||000009||TRiAD||11-01-2001||10:46 PM||||Interesting, I had never heard that explanation of Satan's appearance before. <BR>Just to clarify, when you say "Christian" in that story, you are speaking about today's Catholic church, and not the many, many Prodestant and other groups who have left Catholicism. I'll look into "our" (Christians) explanation of his "popular" appearance. The Bible describes him as "an angel of light" and explains that, as the minister of music/worship in heaven, his body was made of beautiful crystals, and he has a wind, a percussive, and a string instrument built right into his being. (This is all from Isaiah and Psalms). He was one of the 3 Archangels, Michael (the warrior) and Gabriel (the messenger) being the other two. When he rebelled and was thrown from heaven, 1/3 of the angels went with him (forever to be outnumbered, apparently). <P>Anyway...||||reg||1
Z||000010||TRiAD||11-01-2001||10:56 PM||||...for anyone who KNOWS their Wicca, I have a few questions, again, we're all friends here, I'm just curious about your beliefs. You can ask me whatever you want about mine (or any of the others I've studied) as well...<P>When we say "Wicca", "The Church and School of Wicca", "The Religious Order of Witchcraft" (inc, 1972, New Orleans), or simply "witchcraft", we're talking about the same thing, right? ("Larson's ew Book of Cults, (c)1989).<BR>This is loosely related to "Black Magic", "Macumba", and "Voodoo/Santeria", right?<BR>I want to make sure we're all on th same page. <P>The Pentagram and Penticle and Ankh are the symbols, and purpose could be explained as [i]"...to seek the connection between man and his environment...to obtain knowledge. To have the power and to use it to achieve balance. To discover truths...possible unleash the gods and goddesses within us all. Reincarnation, and good and evil being returned (three-fold) via karma are also core beliefs. <BR>Is this right so far?<P>I just want to make sure we have a basis for conversation...<BR>Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000011||mrs. banditbalz||11-01-2001||11:07 PM||||Hi I just wanted to add my piece to this topic I am Wiccan.  Last night I had a samhain dinner with a couple of my friends and we held a small ritual with scying and the simple feast afterward. This was the first time I celebrated with other people it went well I must say. so what did my fellow pagans do to celebrate. <P>Blessed Be!||||reg||7
Z||000012||8Ball||11-02-2001||12:06 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TRiAD:<BR><B><BR>When we say "Wicca", "The Church and School of Wicca", "The Religious Order of Witchcraft" (inc, 1972, New Orleans), or simply "witchcraft", we're talking about the same thing, right? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Yes and no. There are many sects of Wicca and they are as related to each other as the many forms of Christianity.<BR>The church and school of wicca is the Catholic of Wicca IMO<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B><BR>This is loosely related to "Black Magic", "Macumba", and "Voodoo/Santeria", right?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not in any way shape or form are these related.<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B><BR>The Pentagram and Pentacle and Ankh are the symbols, and purpose could be explained as [i]"...to seek the connection between man and his environment...to obtain knowledge. To have the power and to use it to achieve balance. To discover truths...possible unleash the gods and goddesses within us all. Reincarnation, and good and evil being returned (three-fold) via karma are also core beliefs. <BR>Is this right so far?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Basically, Except the Symbol correctly associated with Wicca is the pentacle. The ankh is an egyptian symbol. And the pentagram is commonly associated with satanism.||||reg||1
